{title: I Lay My Sins on Jesus}
{artist: Horatius Bonar / Edmund Sedding}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: F}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Hymns Ancient and Modern, standard edition (Norwich, England: Canterbury Press, 1994), # 769)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]I [Dm]lay my sins on [Gm]Je__[C]__[F]sus,
[C]The [Am]spot[Dm]less [Bb]Lamb of [C]God;
[C]He [F]bears them [C]all, [F]and [Gm]frees__[C7]__ [Dm]us
[Dm]From [Gm]the ac[F]cursèd [C]load;
[Cm]I [Gm]bring__[D]__ my [Gm]guilt to [Cm]Je__[F]__[Bb]sus,
[Bb]To [C]wash my crimson [F]stains
[F]White in His [D7]blood most pre[Gm]cious,
[Gm]Till [C7]not [F]a stain [C]re[F]mains.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]I [Dm]lay my wants on [Gm]Je__[C]__[F]sus;
[C]All [Am]full[Dm]ness [Bb]dwells in [C]Him;
[C]He [F]heals all [C]my [F]dis[Gm]eas__[C7]__[Dm]es,
[Dm]He [Gm]doth my [F]soul re[C]deem:
[Cm]I [Gm]lay__[D]__ my [Gm]griefs on [Cm]Je__[F]__[Bb]sus,
[Bb]My [C]burdens and my [F]cares;
[F]He from them [D7]all releas[Gm]es,
[Gm]He [C7]all [F]my sor[C]rows [F]shares.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]I [Dm]rest my soul on [Gm]Je__[C]__[F]sus,
[C]This [Am]wea[Dm]ry [Bb]soul of [C]mine;
[C]His [F]right hand [C]me [F]em[Gm]brac__[C7]__[Dm]es,
[Dm]I [Gm]on His [F]breast re[C]cline.
[Cm]I [Gm]love__[D]__ the [Gm]name of [Cm]Je__[F]__[Bb]sus,
[Bb]Im[C]manuel, Christ, the [F]Lord;
[F]Like fragrance [D7]on the breez[Gm]es
[Gm]His [C7]name [F]abroad [C]is [F]poured.
{end_of_verse}
